Description: GNOME Shell extension for screenshots, annotation and recording
 CapIt freezes the screen and lets you pick a region, a whole window or a
 panel inside it, then annotate it with arrows, shapes, text, blur and
 redaction before copying it to the clipboard, saving it to a folder, or both.
 It also records a region of the screen as a GIF or an MP4 video.
 .
 It runs on GNOME Shell on Wayland and on Xorg. The capit command opens a
 capture, so it can be bound to a keyboard shortcut.
 .
 Recording needs FFmpeg and the GStreamer plugins this package recommends.
